WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.569
-Our first guest tonight
is an Emmy-nominated

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:04.704
and Tony Award-winning actor
you know from shows

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:07.206
such as "Schmigadoon!"
and "The Good Wife."

00:00:07.206 --> 00:00:09.242
He is currently starring
in "Burn,"

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:10.943
which is playing at
the Joyce theater.

00:00:10.943 --> 00:00:13.946
And he also starred in the final
season of "The Good Fight."

00:00:13.946 --> 00:00:16.015
New episodes stream Thursdays
on Paramount+.

00:00:16.015 --> 00:00:17.016
Please welcome back to the show,

00:00:17.016 --> 00:00:18.751
our friend Alan Cumming,
everybody!

00:00:18.751 --> 00:00:21.754
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.754 --> 00:00:26.959 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:26.959 --> 00:00:32.165 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:34.834
-Look at how monochromatic
we both are.

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:37.070
-I know, right?
-It's very lovely.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.871
-And it's -- it's the first day
of autumn,

00:00:38.871 --> 00:00:41.074
so I'm going for a cozy look.

00:00:41.074 --> 00:00:42.776
-It's very cozy.
You look very cozy.

00:00:42.776 --> 00:00:43.910
-Thanks.
-So, this is --

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:45.444
you're doing a one-man show
right now,

00:00:45.444 --> 00:00:48.481
which historically are known
to be exhausting

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:50.316
for the people on stage.
-Oh, do you think?

00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:51.617
-You've got to do it all
yourself.

00:00:51.617 --> 00:00:52.919
-Yes.
-And there's an element

00:00:52.919 --> 00:00:54.420
of dance?

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:55.755
-[ Laughs ] Yes.

00:00:55.755 --> 00:00:57.390
-You've done this to yourself,
as well, we should note.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.926
-And it was my idea.
I have no one to blame.

00:00:59.926 --> 00:01:02.528
So, I mean,
I'm nearly finished it.

00:01:02.528 --> 00:01:05.831
And it's sort of -- I mean, you
just hurt when you're dancing.

00:01:05.831 --> 00:01:07.400
You just hurt.
Things -- right now,

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.068
I'm hurting in front of you.

00:01:09.068 --> 00:01:11.537
-[ Laughs ]
-And it's --

00:01:11.537 --> 00:01:13.506
I know. You know, and also,
I'm getting older.

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:14.840
I'm not -- I shouldn't be --

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:18.611
like, this is sort
of my dance theater debut at 57.

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:20.446
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.446 --> 00:01:22.248
I know, it's hard to believe.
-Very few people.

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:23.382
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:23.382 --> 00:01:24.483
-I know. I know.
-Very few people break into

00:01:24.483 --> 00:01:26.853
the stage dance game that late.

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:28.254
-It's just mental.

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:31.958
And so, I have had -- you know,
I wake up and I'm like,

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:34.360
"Oh, ouch,"
and funny things happen.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:38.230
And just -- I've got sore arms.
I don't know why.

00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:40.566
-Do you do a lot of arm movement
during you're dancing?

00:01:40.566 --> 00:01:42.134
-I guess I must do it.

00:01:42.134 --> 00:01:45.772
And then I bang myself on the
table, and I have to jump.

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:47.573
It's just a lot of stuff
going on.

00:01:47.573 --> 00:01:49.509
-Now, the other interesting
thing about having

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:52.112
all this element of movement,
is it is a one-man show

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:54.180
about a Scottish poet,
Robert Burns.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.516
I think if you heard there
was a one-man show

00:01:56.516 --> 00:01:58.384
about a Scottish poet,
you might not think

00:01:58.384 --> 00:01:59.685
there'd be that much dancing.
-You'd think there might

00:01:59.685 --> 00:02:01.454
be poetry.
-Yeah.

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:02.655
-Well, there's a little bit
of poetry.

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:04.390
I mean, I speak in it as well.

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:06.859
But I sort of -- like, what I
wanted to do with this show,

00:02:06.859 --> 00:02:09.662
because Robert Burns
is this huge icon in Scotland.

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:11.464
He's our national bard.

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:13.499
And I wanted -- I found out lots
of things about him

00:02:13.499 --> 00:02:14.833
that were really surprising
to me.

00:02:14.833 --> 00:02:17.803
About the fact that he was
bipolar and he had this --

00:02:17.803 --> 00:02:19.706
you know, was much more fragile
and had this terrible life.

00:02:19.706 --> 00:02:23.042
And so, I'm asking -- I'm asking
the audience to sort of think,

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:26.045
especially in Scotland, where we
did it first, to think again,

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:29.048
about someone that you have all
these preconceived ideas about.

00:02:29.048 --> 00:02:32.318
So, I thought, in a way,
if I did that in a form

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:34.921
that was not something they were
used to seeing me doing,

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:36.322
then that would sort of help.

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:39.525
So the dance thing kind of helps
you break down your barriers

00:02:39.525 --> 00:02:41.160
and receive new information.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:42.862
Because you're so like,
"What the [bleep] is going on?

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:44.664
Alan Cumming's dancing."

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:46.632
-I -- well, I also heard
to prepare for this role,

00:02:46.632 --> 00:02:49.902
because it was physically
and emotionally taxing,

00:02:49.902 --> 00:02:51.337
that you stopped drinking
for a while.

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:52.338
How did that go?

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:53.773
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.773 --> 00:02:56.309
-I think your research is a
little lacking, sorry to say,

00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:57.310
but --

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:58.511
[ Laughter ]

00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:00.179
-You went one evening?
-It was about two nights,

00:03:00.179 --> 00:03:01.247
I think, I might --

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:02.281
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.281 --> 00:03:03.682
-Two nights?!
-Because then I'd --

00:03:03.682 --> 00:03:05.517
I honestly thought, and then
when I came home and I was like,

00:03:05.517 --> 00:03:07.687
"Ow, oh, oh."
I went, "Oh, I'm not allowed --

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:09.222
Oh, [bleep] that,
I'm going to have a drink."

00:03:09.222 --> 00:03:10.390
Sorry, I keep swearing.

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:11.891
-I think the problem
you should worry about

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:13.993
is that you stopped
drinking for two days

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:16.162
and it was such news that it
made it to our research team.

00:03:16.162 --> 00:03:19.064
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.064 --> 00:03:21.200
Everybody was walking
around Broadway being like,

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.501
"Did you hear about Alan?"
-"What?!

00:03:22.501 --> 00:03:24.570
Alan Cumming stopped drinking?"
-"48 hours."

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:27.239
-"I know. Is he all right?"

00:03:27.239 --> 00:03:29.742
Like, that's terrible.
Yeah, no, I think I had to --

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:31.077
you know, you have to --

00:03:31.077 --> 00:03:33.713
I mean, I've lost weight,
and my body is doing

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:37.016
all these things, and it's been
an incredible experience.

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:39.151
And you know, I've got these
funny hair extensions.

00:03:39.151 --> 00:03:40.286
My nails are black.

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:42.855
There's a whole new vibe
I'm going for with this,

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:44.957
but the one constant
was vodka soda,

00:03:44.957 --> 00:03:46.225
just to get me through
the thing.

00:03:46.225 --> 00:03:47.760
-Yeah, that's good.
We appreciate your honesty.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.228
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:49.228 --> 00:03:51.397
You know, obviously,
I don't need to tell you

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:53.699
because it was well-covered --
the Queen recently passed away.

00:03:53.699 --> 00:03:55.068
-What?!
-And yeah -- Oh, no.

00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:56.301
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.301 --> 00:03:58.037
-Is that how deep you've
been in your one-man show?

00:03:58.037 --> 00:04:00.306
[ Laughter ]

00:04:00.306 --> 00:04:02.875
-I've been in a "Burn" cave.

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:05.311
-Did you -- a lot of people
have been sharing anecdotes

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:07.913
about meeting the Queen,
crossing paths.

00:04:07.913 --> 00:04:10.249
Did you ever -- did you ever
have the pleasure?

00:04:10.249 --> 00:04:12.251
-I never properly met her.
I met a lot of them.

00:04:12.251 --> 00:04:16.722
Like, I met Prince Charles when
I did that film "Golden Eye,"

00:04:16.722 --> 00:04:17.756
the James Bond one.

00:04:17.756 --> 00:04:19.725
He was --
It was the Royal premiere night,

00:04:19.725 --> 00:04:22.428
and you get all these pages
of etiquette for things.

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:24.063
And I was standing next
to Judi Dench,

00:04:24.063 --> 00:04:26.733
and I said "I'm not bowing.
I'm not bowing. Are you bowing?"

00:04:26.733 --> 00:04:28.868
And she was like, "I have
to bow. I'm a dame."

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:30.002
I was like, "Oh, all right."

00:04:30.002 --> 00:04:31.304
And then, but it said --

00:04:31.304 --> 00:04:33.305
But on the the etiquette,
it said men must bow

00:04:33.305 --> 00:04:34.606
from the neck forward.

00:04:34.606 --> 00:04:35.641
I was like, "Well, you're hardly
going to bow

00:04:35.641 --> 00:04:36.775
from the neck back."

00:04:36.775 --> 00:04:40.112
[ Laughter ]
So -- We -- It was --

00:04:40.112 --> 00:04:42.749
-Like a Pez dispenser.
-Yes.

00:04:42.749 --> 00:04:45.585
And so, on the news there was
like, there's Prince Charles

00:04:45.585 --> 00:04:47.353
and Pierce Brosnan,
and in the background,

00:04:47.353 --> 00:04:49.288
you see me and Judi Dench
laughing and going like this --

00:04:49.288 --> 00:04:52.558
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.558 --> 00:04:55.961
-But I -- one time when I was
in the Scouts,

00:04:55.961 --> 00:04:58.263
like the Boy Scouts,
and we were --

00:04:58.263 --> 00:04:59.932
-So, this is when you were
younger?

00:04:59.932 --> 00:05:01.334
-Yes.
-Yeah.

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:03.703
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.703 --> 00:05:05.504
-Imagine if I was still
in the Scouts now.

00:05:05.504 --> 00:05:06.772
That would be hilarious.

00:05:06.772 --> 00:05:08.073
Where's I'm hiking, you know,

00:05:08.073 --> 00:05:11.510
I'm orienteering or something in
Deeside in Aberdeenshire,

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:14.346
which is near Balmoral,
and so it was raining

00:05:14.346 --> 00:05:15.414
and we were lost.

00:05:15.414 --> 00:05:17.015
And I was, like,
the patrol leader.

00:05:17.015 --> 00:05:18.517
And I said,
"Oh, I can't deal with this.

00:05:18.517 --> 00:05:20.018
It's not my forte."

00:05:20.018 --> 00:05:23.355
And so, we saw this Land Rover
coming along this little track,

00:05:23.355 --> 00:05:25.124
and I said,
"Well, let's just hitch a lift.

00:05:25.124 --> 00:05:26.258
They'll take pity on us.

00:05:26.258 --> 00:05:28.760
We're all bedraggled
and wet-looking scouts."

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:31.797
It was the Queen
in a Land Rover,

00:05:31.797 --> 00:05:33.399
and she didn't blooming well
stop.

00:05:33.399 --> 00:05:35.067
[ Laughter ]

00:05:35.067 --> 00:05:37.203
We were like...

00:05:37.203 --> 00:05:39.305
We were like, "Oh,
it's the Queen. Hi!"

00:05:39.305 --> 00:05:41.140
[ Laughter ]

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:42.241
So, that is my claim to fame,

00:05:42.241 --> 00:05:44.043
that the Queen did not
pick me up.

00:05:44.043 --> 00:05:46.145
-All right. Well, thank you
for sharing a story,

00:05:46.145 --> 00:05:48.113
because I feel like right now,
maybe a lot of the stories

00:05:48.113 --> 00:05:51.383
are inflating her kindness,
and it's nice to get --

00:05:51.383 --> 00:05:53.252
-Balance.
-Yeah, get a little balance.

00:05:53.252 --> 00:05:55.187
-Balance is everything.
-I have more to ask you.

00:05:55.187 --> 00:05:57.757
We'll be right back with
Alan Cumming, everybody.

